title: "Finite Contact Theory v0.10: Negative-Gram Identity Holonomy — The Program's First Divergence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Douglas"
    given-names: "Seth"
    email: "apsiape@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/finite-contact-theory-public"
abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program, now spanning ten chapters: three recovery lines and a first extension line. The recovery lines grow the Bell/CHSH boundary, rational Born weights, a native carrier grammar, an exact preparation gap, the identifiability and debt calculus, the inquiry calculus, four theorems on time, a measured generative floor, a quaternionic contact-interface cell whose closure is the 24-cell and F_4 with a finite Gleason theorem and a triality Kochen-Specker obstruction (Chapter 8), and a multi-floor forcing audit recovering the E_8-hexacode spine while proving the floor forces the atlas of lawful closures and the terminal self-dual class but never the specific member (Chapter 9). This v0.10 chapter is the program's FIRST EXTENSION, and it recovers nothing: it predicts a possible violation of Hilbert-space positivity. Two things are held rigidly apart. (A) An UNCONDITIONAL theorem: a three-contact class function with a negative sign-sector eigenvalue nonetheless keeps every passive-linear-optical probability nonnegative -- the accessible amplitudes are the monomials of one complex 3x3 interferometer matrix, obeying prod_even z = prod_odd z, and at r = 3/5 the exact inequality 152||z||^2 + 9|per A|^2 - 36|det A|^2 >= (7/2)||z||^2 holds for every A -- so the sector is a lawful probabilistic model that lies OUTSIDE the positive-semidefinite Hilbert Gram cone. (B) A CONDITIONAL, preregistered, experiment-open prediction: on the received anchor r = 3/5 and the odd Z_2 identity-holonomy sector (Phi = pi), the three-state Gram discriminant Delta_3 = (1-2r)(1+r)^2 = -64/125 is negative, where ordinary quantum mechanics forces Delta_3 >= 0, and the registered joint count vector (Delta_3, W, Q_3) both excludes the PSD Gram class and rejects the pairwise-only null (Q_3 = 0). This is a registered bet with a protocol and kill conditions, not a discovery; the bridge premises (a particle class carrying Z_2 identity holonomy; photons receiving it, with anyonic/topological matter the natural home; passive linear optics as the complete grammar) are held open, and the mixed-state PSD-exclusion is an open crux awaiting an external quantum-optics expert. This DOI is an archival priority record, not an empirical discovery. One dependency-free script verifies the chapter from a clean clone in exact arithmetic."
